## California Lemon Law: Also for Used Cars in Cathedral City

Apart from new cars, the **lemon law in California** also applies to pre-owned vehicles if they come with a warranty.

## Warranties on Used Cars from Dealerships

When you buy a used car from a dealership, it often comes with a warranty that lasts up to 30 days or 1,000 miles- whichever comes first. If your car starts acting up during this period, you might be covered under California lemon law.

What You Can Claim If Your Used Car is a Lemon

As per California law, you might be able to file for a buyback if your used car has issues the dealership can’t fix under warranty. Here’s what you can typically claim:

- The full purchase price of the vehicle

- Any official fees related to the vehicle

- Additional costs you’ve incurred

- All your legal and attorney fees

What it Means to Buy a Car ‘As-Is’ in California

Buying a car “[as is](https://www.hg.org/legal-articles/as-is-vehicles-36501)” in Cathedral City means you agree to take it with all its existing issues, which might limit your lemon law rights. However, this only applies if the dealership clearly explains that the car is being sold “as is.” If they don’t disclose this information at the time of the sale, you could still have a lemon law claim.

